      "message": "Rewriting the function as a single ternary expression makes the inliner very happy. (The original code couldn\u0027t inline at all due to early returns.)\n\nSkSL actually surprised me by optimizing away one of ternaries entirely--look at the minified output and you will see it boiled the expression down to `return isinf(p23.z) ? $kTriangularConicCurveType : float(isinf(p23.w));`. This uses the optimization pattern of `boolExpr ? 1.0 : 0.0` --\u003e `float(boolExpr)`.",
